was with great sadness that West Michigan learned on Friday of the passing of our first lady, Betty Ford. The first lady spent most of her life in Grand Rapids. A graduate of Central High School, she worked in a department store downtown and was a dance instructor. Early on, Mrs. Ford showed her heart for the disadvantage in our community, teaching dance to children who are physically disabled, deaf, and blind.

[[00:00:28.410]]
